 "engine": "argonautlabsai/argodrive-ds4-kimi-k3.1, commit bb5c53b6f4d4602247e9f8950303fbf43e5175a6 (tag k31-cuda-20261111)",
 "build_note": "the runs were made with a build of these sources before one source comment was corrected; all 15 object files of the tagged commit have the same code sections as that build",
 "previous_release": "commit fd65719 (tag k31-cuda-20261110). Run beside this release on the same drives the same night, with its own sidecar, for the 512-token generation, prompt-512-tokens.txt, a code prompt and two everyday prompts (beside_previous_release), and plain for two rows (previous_release_runs); its other rows are in kimi-k31-2026-11-10.json",
 "changes": "scheduling, caching, buffers and block width only, no arithmetic change: verification blocks of up to 64 rows (DS4_K3_QWEN_ROWS), a block wider than 32 rows using the prompt pass's compact partials with each row's slots in ascending expert id and keeping its per-layer KDA inputs in host memory between layers (DS4_K3_QWEN_KIN_ROWS); the sidecar goes past 32 rows only when the product of Qwen's confidences over the first 31 drafts is at least 0.5 (DS4_K3_QWEN_WIDE), keeps the rows it has computed (DS4_K3_QWEN_KEEP) and prepares the deep rows only after a proposal of at least 16 drafts (DS4_K3_QWEN_SPEC_MIN); a block admits only experts that at least 20 % of its rows use (DS4_K3_VERIFY_ADMIT_PCT); prompt passes read up to 768 more of the next layer's predicted experts into the host pool alone (DS4_K3_PREFILL_PREFETCH_HOST); the prompt pass's compact partials are freed when generation starts. Fix: a decode step's dense partials are allocated before the expert cache takes the free VRAM, a failed GPU step ends the run with an error, and the sidecar caps the history it gives Qwen (DS4_K3_QWEN_CTX, 4096) and survives an out-of-memory forward",
 "drafter": "Qwen/Qwen3-0.6B-Base, revision da87bfb608c14b7cf20ba1ce41287e8de496c0cd, float16 on the same GPU; proposals of 2 to 63 tokens make blocks of up to 64 rows; on raw text the gate starts at 0.6 and adapts within 0.6 to 0.95",
 "hardware": "one RTX PRO 6000 Blackwell (96 GB) in a 70 GiB VM; RAID0 of three NVMe with 79,365 experts; second NVMe with 11,768 (the other 3,067 plus 8,701 copies); the Thunderbolt NVMe of the 6 to 8 November runs was not attached",
 "settings": "documented defaults, DS4_K3_TRACE_HASH=1, -c 2048 for the standard rows, greedy, one fresh process per run; long-context rows with DS4_K3_DSA=<indexer file>, DS4_K3_CACHE_CAP and -c equal to the context; raw mode except the chat rows, which use the chat template with DS4_K3_QWEN_CHAT=1 DS4_K3_QWEN_CONF=0.9",
